1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,000
A node can’t store current.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,800
What goes in, comes out.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,900
6.4 minus 2.6: 3.8 A in the other branch.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,300
The source gives 48 V. R1 drops 20 V.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,800
Around the loop, the sum is zero.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,900
48 minus 20: 28 V across R2.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,800
When fault-finding, your readings must add up the same way.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,900
If they don’t, you’ve found where the fault is.

9
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,900
In equals out. Around the loop is zero.
